Here is an example method that does this:
```
public static Map<DataType, List<Data>> classifyData(List<Data> dataList) {
    Map<DataType, List<Data>> classifiedData = new HashMap<>();
    for(Data data : dataList) {
        if(!classifiedData.containsKey(data.getType())) {
            classifiedData.put(data.getType(), new ArrayList<>());
        }
        classifiedData.get(data.getType()).add(data);
    }
    return classifiedData;
}
```
This method takes in a list of Data objects and returns a Map where the keys are the DataType values and the values are lists of Data objects that have that DataType. You can then use this Map to easily access and manipulate the classified data.
