   ```

   You can then analyze the stress patterns to determine the meter and rhyme scheme of each poem. For example, if both poems have a regular iambic meter, you can note that as a similarity between the two poems.
7. Identify underlying themes and messages:
   To identify underlying themes and messages, you can use a topic modeling algorithm such as Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA). Here's an example of how to use the lda library to extract topics from the poems:
